Dear {{CUSTOMER_NAME}},

Thank you for contacting Meridian Harbor Bank about {{ISSUE_SUMMARY}}. We have opened case {{CASE_ID}} and begun an investigation.

Because your concern involves a disputed transaction, specific federal timeframes apply to our review. We will complete our investigation and write to you with the outcome. If our review takes longer than the initial period allowed, we will tell you what interim steps apply to your account.

You do not need to do anything further right now. If you have documents that would help — such as a receipt or a screenshot — you can reply to this message and they will be added to the case.

{{NEXT_STEP}}

Sincerely,
{{ANALYST_NAME}}
{{DEPARTMENT_LABEL}}
Meridian Harbor Bank

Dear {{CUSTOMER_NAME}},

Thank you for writing to us about {{ISSUE_SUMMARY}}. We have opened case {{CASE_ID}}.

A member of our {{DEPARTMENT_LABEL}} team is reviewing the fees assessed on your account and the disclosures that applied to them. We will write to you with what we find and, where a fee was applied in error, what we are doing about it.

{{NEXT_STEP}}

Sincerely,
{{ANALYST_NAME}}
{{DEPARTMENT_LABEL}}
Meridian Harbor Bank

Dear {{CUSTOMER_NAME}},

Thank you for telling us what is happening. We have opened case {{CASE_ID}} about {{ISSUE_SUMMARY}}, and I want you to know a person is looking at it rather than a queue.

A member of our {{DEPARTMENT_LABEL}} team will contact you directly. If there is a deadline on your side that we should know about, reply to this message and tell us the date — we will work to it.

{{NEXT_STEP}}

Sincerely,
{{ANALYST_NAME}}
{{DEPARTMENT_LABEL}}
Meridian Harbor Bank

Dear {{CUSTOMER_NAME}},

Thank you for contacting Meridian Harbor Bank about {{ISSUE_SUMMARY}}. We have opened case {{CASE_ID}} and routed it to our {{DEPARTMENT_LABEL}} team.

We are reviewing what happened and will write to you with what we find. If you would like to add anything to the case, you can reply to this message.

{{NEXT_STEP}}

Sincerely,
